LED MATRIX / FRAMEBUFFER CONTROL

The teaching board has an 8x8 LED matrix. Multiple programs may
compete for its GPIOs; stop conflicting demos before changes.

INSPECT
  pins
  help fbctl
  fbctl status

BOUNDED OPERATIONS
  fbctl on
  fbctl clear
  fbctl test
  fbctl off
Run a state-changing operation only after approval and verify
when possible. Test patterns may temporarily take over LEDs.

TEXT SCROLLING
  echo HELLO | scroll
  scroll -u 2001       UDP listener; long-running
Simple stdin piping is preferable to starting a UDP server via
MCP. Still verify the foreground command completes within the
MCP tool timeout before relying on it.

INTERACTIVE EDITORS
  fbed, gpio, mem, vi, edit, fd and watch use a terminal.
  Never start these in MCP execute_command.

LIMITATIONS
  Framebuffer control and text scroll may claim the matrix pins.
  A second app can conflict or cause unexpected appearance.
  Check /dev/fb availability and console before operation.
